WEBVTT

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.030
We don't have time to waste on the fighters.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.520
Let's do this quick!

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.270
Enemy craft at two o' clock.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.150
Five o' clock, too.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.120
They're on both sides of us?

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.250
Kei, fire.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.110
It will hit.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.240
They're behind us!

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:19.860
Fire.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.670
It hit!

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.870
It's fine.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.990
I can take down most enemies 
within our firing range.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.720
Seriously?

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.510
<i>Kei-san, conserve your missiles.</i>

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.930
<i>Ready guns. The next ones 
are coming in from above.</i>

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:38.800
A-Above?

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.040
<i>Pitch up.</i>

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.800
Right!

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.880
<i>Adjust throttle.</i>

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.860
<i>Right.</i>

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.610
<i>Fox 3!</i>

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:52.920
Wow...

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:56.160
This definitely isn't my piloting, though!

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.770
<i>Remember that feeling.</i>

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.780
I'm not a puppet!

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.550
But that feeling...

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.500
Where are they coming from?

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.790
Kei, below us!

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.840
New units. From the island.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.080
The SAM cluster rounds?!

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.270
Phantom, circle around the 
island and try to evade them!

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.740
Second wave, incoming.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.270
Crap!

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.750
Third wave.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.030
There's no end to them...

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.670
We can't protect Phantom like this.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.600
Barbie 04?

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.280
Viper Zero.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.830
She destroyed the enemy air defense 
network with an NOE bombing run.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.980
I have ASuW capability as well,

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.260
but I can't carry that kind of firepower.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.080
She really is a pervert.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.920
She's gone.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.330
The threat has passed.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.870
Let's get started.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.360
Can I trust you to protect me?

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.910
Yes. I won't let a single 
one get close to you!

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.210
You'll have front-row seats 
to watch my performance.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.980
<i>Oh my. How cool.</i>

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.040
Barbie 03 to Dollhouse.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.830
Ready for control.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:04.820
Request permission to begin mission.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:05.840
<i>Roger.</i>

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.290
<i>Survivors of the 7th Fleet</i>

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.670
<i>Ishigaki Island</i>

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.880
<i>JGSDF Artillery Regiment</i>

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.580
Wow...

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.030
EPCM levels dropping.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.960
Surviving Xi are retreating.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.640
Is it over?

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:03.480
Yes.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.480
Eagle safely protected the fleet, too.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.670
This mission was a big success,

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.400
and I did just what she told me.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.600
I took control.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.100
Okay!

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.680
Let's get back.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.720
Mission complete! RTB!

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:30.560
Take that!

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.200
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.470
Do I?

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.470
You've got a full lineup 
of extra large, medium,

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.380
and petite to choose from.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.890
What?

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.550
I'm kidding.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:52.270
Thanks to you, we were able 
to complete our mission.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.210
To be honest, I expected to 
lose an Anima out there.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.250
So this was the best possible outcome.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.400
Phantom?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.110
That aside,

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:05.210
pilot Narutani Kei with fire control 
and radar officer Gripen...

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.370
It worked out pretty well, didn't it?

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.580
You can hit any enemy in your 
firing range with a missile,

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.140
Wait for me!

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.120
regardless of their exact location.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.360
With that sort of advantage, a small loss 
of maneuverability isn't a problem.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:19.070
So it all worked out like you planned?

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:23.950
No, I just bet on one of those 
"new possibilities" you talked about.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.690
Kei-san, why do you think that girls 
like us, made from parts of the Xi,

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:33.600
are allowed autonomy?

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:38.880
The natural choice would have been 
to have the Anima support humans.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:44.480
It feels to me like you two 
are the right way to do this.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:49.800
You may be the key to winning this war.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.490
Come and get me!

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.250
We're the key?

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.350
If you ever feel like having a new partner,

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.780
I'll be waiting.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:05.040
I won, so that's not happening, right?

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.360
I wouldn't force you.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:15.200
But I think I can show you some 
things you'll never see with her.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.520
Die.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:59.040
<i>An Unhappy Top Secret</i>

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:55.900
Hey!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.000
<b>Yashirodoori-san (JSDF)</b>

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.000
<b>Emergency</b>

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.000
<b>Sending a car</b>

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.000
<b>Inbox</b>

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.680
<i>Emergency. Sending a car.</i>

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:06.770
Seriously?

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.770
What?!

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.430
<i>Naha Base</i>

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:18.170
And now I'm back in Okinawa.

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:23.890
Sorry, there was a screw-up and some 
parts for Gripen ended up coming here.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:28.530
It would take too long to get a plane 
ready to get them sent to Komatsu,

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:31.600
so the director said to just do the 
work here and bring them back.

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:33.910
You guys are as crazy as ever.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.700
Everyone makes mistakes.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.020
It's not their fault.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:40.610
But who sends a fighter plane up 
into the air to correct a mistake?

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.890
You were able to get to Okinawa from your 
house in 30 minutes because of that.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.120
You should save stunts
 like that for a hot scramble!

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:49.850
How long is this going to take?

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:52.360
What, did you have plans?

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:54.170
No, not really.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:57.130
Probably not that long.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:01.760
Kei, I need tuning and have 
to stay here for a while.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:02.600
What do you want to do?

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.010
I'll just go for a walk.

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.340
Call my phone if you need something.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.230
Sure, thanks.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>Minghua</b>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>Yesterday</b>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>How much longer?</b>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>Sorry, I lost track of time.
I'll be back around 6:40.</b>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>That's super late! I needed you to
 buy some groceries, but forget it!</b>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>How would I know that?!</b>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>Could you buy some cabbages after all?</b>

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.660
<b>Sure...</b>

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.700
No word from her, huh?

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:28.440
M-Minghua?

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:31.010
Minghua! Minghua!

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:33.770
Wh-What are you doing here?

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.550
And that outfit...

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.650
Did somebody bring you here?

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.560
Um, well...

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.510
There's a reason I'm dressed like this.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:46.870
It was kind of an accident.
Not really my fault...

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:49.020
And I was piloting that f-fighter because...

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.910
O-Or well, it's kind of a fighter...

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.250
I mean, it's a normal aircraft!

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.300
And it was because somebody 
from the base told me to!

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.640
So you don't need to worry.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.530
I'm not planning on joining the military.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:05.340
H-Hey, Minghua!

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:09.650
What's your problem today?

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:15.930
Hey, Kei,

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.420
do you still want to go see that movie?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.730
Movie?

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:20.010
Jeez!

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.760
This one!

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.290
Our favorite actor is in it.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.170
We were talking about going to see it!

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:29.880
Oh, that was a great movie.

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:32.620
I love that actor.

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:34.770
You should go see it if you get a chance.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:37.160
Who'd you go with?

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.260
A friend. Yesterday.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:44.770
Listen, I didn't go with my 
friend because you invited me.

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:47.140
If you didn't want to go together, 
you should've said so.

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.230
That's really mean.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.660
Huh?

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:52.130
I never said I was going with you.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:55.010
If you wanted to go, 
you should've said something.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:57.820
You're the one who brought it up!

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.960
"There's this great movie out.
 I want to go see it."

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:04.470
That's why I said to myself, 
"Oh, I bet he wants to go with me!"

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:08.000
I just told you about a movie!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.800
You're the one who got the wrong idea!

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:11.880
So you're saying it's my fault?

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.480
It's not anybody's fault.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.670
You're just being weird.

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:21.260
Fine. If I see something I think 
you'll like, I just won't tell you.

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:22.390
That's what you want, right?

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:27.040
Why are you being so mean?

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:30.610
I was looking forward to it.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:36.540
I'm sorry.

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:38.830
We're living together, after all.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:42.610
It would be weird to find out about 
something fun and not tell you.

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:47.210
From now on, I'll make sure to add, 
"Go see it with somebody else."

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:48.950
That's fine, right?

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:51.780
Die.

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:56.760
Listen, Minghua.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.330
Are you still mad?

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:02.050
<i>I don't want to fight with you.</i>

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:04.320
<i>I want to be friends.</i>

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.480
<i>But she keeps crying and picking fights...</i>

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:10.010
<i>I don't understand her.</i>

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.870
<i>She and I used to get 
in fights all the time.</i>

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:18.590
<i>But as time passed, we always made up.</i>

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:20.400
Don't worry!

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.900
Big Sis Minghua is here for you!

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:25.200
You don't have to worry about a thing.

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:29.260
Listen, Minghua.

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:31.220
I don't know how to handle this, either.

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:34.040
I don't know what you're thinking.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:37.360
Have I done something to upset 
you without realizing it?

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:44.360
<b>Text Memo</b>

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:44.360
<b>Do you want to improve your
 relationship with this person?</b>

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:43.720
"Do you want to improve your 
relationship with this person?"

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:47.100
"This person"? I'm talking about you.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.680
Well, we've known each other a long time.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:52.850
So I don't want you to hate me.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:59.210
<b>Text Memo</b>

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:59.210
<b>Then tell me
 the details</b>

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:59.200
"Then tell me the details."

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:02.440
Why are you typing into your phone, anyway?

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:08.930
<b>Yummy
</b>Delicious Shaved Ice

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:18.980
<b>Text Memo</b>

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:18.980
<b>Then there is nothing to
 be concerned about.
She considered you
 special from a biological
 perspective, that is,
 as a partner in passing
 on her genes</b>

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:11.450
"Then there is nothing 
to be concerned about.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:15.210
She considered you special from 
a biological perspective,

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:18.940
that is, as a partner in 
passing on her genes...?"

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.570
A partner in passing on her genes?!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:22.970
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.740
Do you have a fever?

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:25.900
Are you insane?

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.600
Also, would you talk to me already?

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.800
What do I have to do for you to forgive me?

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.920
<b>Text Memo</b>

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.920
<b>Go see 
another movie</b>

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:37.900
"Go see another movie"?

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:41.310
But you said you wanted to see that movie.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.380
"That's just an excuse"?

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:47.430
"What's important is to experience 
the same thing together"?

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.250
"It's important that you're together"?

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:52.270
Listen, what's gotten into you?

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:55.620
Th-This is, um...

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:58.010
This is you saying you like me, right?

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:02.280
But to me, you're more like a big 
sister I can count on.

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:04.880
Let me think!

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.360
<b>Text Memo</b>

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.360
<b>Think about it until you're satisfied.
The choice is yours to make.</b>

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.360
<b>Problems with your condition affect
the combat power of autonomous 
flight unit #4. If left unfixed,
this could threaten operational efforts.</b>

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.070
"The choice is mine to make"?

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.020
That's not fair!

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:17.370
"Problems with your condition affect the 
combat power of autonomous flight unit #4."

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:21.430
"If left unfixed, this could 
threaten operational efforts."

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.710
You're really Minghua, right?

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:28.550
Oh, Narutani-kun! There you are.

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:32.410
I don't know why she's here, either!

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:34.060
I definitely didn't—

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.360
What are you talking about? Nobody's there.

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:38.320
Huh?

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:41.730
I tried integrating the 
new parts with Gripen,

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.290
but they're not working
 like we thought they would.

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:46.020
I'm taking a little break.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:49.280
I want the pilot's opinion, 
too, so head back.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.420
W-Wait!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.080
Hey, Minghua! Where did you go?

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.110
Stop wandering around!

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:01.620
Come back!

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.830
<i>That's my line!</i>

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:07.080
You run out of the house 
and vanish for hours,

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:08.950
and then you want to know where I went?

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:11.600
So that's how you want 
to do this, huh? Fine!

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.210
I'll come to you right now. 
Tell me where you are.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.260
<i>Are you at home, Minghua?</i>

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:19.740
Of course I am!

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:22.160
Fine. We can talk when I get back.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:24.230
I'm hanging up now! We'll talk later!

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.030
<b>Minghua</b>

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.030
Call Time

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.030
<i>Hey, Kei!</i>

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:29.220
What's going on?

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.200
<b>Komatsu
 Airbase</b>

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:35.900
That was probably Viper Zero.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.790
<b>No Smoking</b>

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:38.780
Huh? Um, Yashirodoori-san...

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:41.360
That was Minghua I saw!

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:44.490
But Minghua-san never left Komatsu, right?

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:47.140
You ran into somebody else in Naha.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:50.550
From what you said about her clothing,
I'm 99% sure that was her.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.750
She likes dressing up.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:56.400
You made contact with the F-2A Anima.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:58.520
F-2A?

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:00.300
Viper Zero...

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.980
But that doesn't make sense!

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:09.480
Why does the F-2A look like Minghua?

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:12.450
That Anima's a little special.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.950
It doesn't have a single form.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.870
Or well, to be more precise,

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.870
it does have an original form, 
but it can't be observed.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:23.400
How it looks depends on who's looking at it.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.080
It changes how it looks?

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:28.750
It's similar to the 
observation selection effect

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:31.140
you read about in the philosophy of science.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:35.630
When a phenomenon is observed,
the characteristics and abilities

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:38.090
of the observer create a bias 
in the observation results.

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:41.720
Recording her with machines or photographing 
her with a camera doesn't help, either.

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:44.480
Whenever a human's subjective 
vision comes into play,

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.580
she'll take the form of whoever the 
viewer thinks about the most.

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:50.350
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:53.190
An illusion? Some kind of hypnosis?

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.160
We don't know how it works.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.620
Her core itself is unstable.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:02.150
An Anima's EGG is supposed to be stable, 
but hers is constantly changing.

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:05.410
She's like a mirror, you could say.

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:09.370
A screen that reflects the heart 
of the person looking at her.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:12.170
Then what I saw...

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.560
...was a reflection of your mind.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:19.050
Of course, she can't copy someone's 
personality or knowledge.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:23.140
Well? How does it feel to 
have touched our top secret?

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:27.490
I made somebody crazy like 
that worry about me?

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:31.300
So why did she look like Minghua-san to you?

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.020
What do you mean?

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:37.480
I told you, she responds to the 
emotions of those she meets.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:40.470
For example, if you're 
starting to develop feelings

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:43.450
for your pretty childhood friend...

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.650
No! No way! You've got the wrong idea!
 It's not like that!

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:50.600
We got into a real fight for 
the first time in years,

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.910
and I wasn't sure what to do. That's all.

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:56.790
Yashirodoori-san, what about you?

00:17:56.790 --> 00:18:00.880
Does Viper Zero look like 
somebody special to you?

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:02.430
An ex-girlfriend or something?

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.290
I'm afraid there's no space

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:08.940
in my brain for remembering 
girls I've broken up with.

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:14.750
But when I see her, I do realize 
that I've lived a complicated life.

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:16.750
It's not a bad feeling.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:22.780
It makes you realize that the path you've 
walked wasn't always through a wasteland.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.660
What does that mean?

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:29.800
Well, someday I'll tell 
you about it over drinks.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:39.840
I'm bac—

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:43.640
Welcome back.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:47.110
You're late... aren't you?

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.160
Y-Yeah...

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.970
You left without even doing the dishes.

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:53.640
Yeah.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:56.850
And you made that weird phone call.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:58.310
Sorry.

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:01.810
You're going to explain where you 
were and what you were doing, right?

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:07.260
Forget it.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:10.170
You've been gone all day, 
and you have to be tired, right?

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.450
Come on in.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:14.770
I'm sure you haven't eaten dinner.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:17.630
It'll just take me a second to warm it up.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.460
You're not mad?

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:36.060
Of course I'm mad.

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.230
Yeah...

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:43.820
But I'd be madder if you hadn't come back.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.480
Um, Minghua...

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:46.700
Wh-What?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:50.200
I could've come home earlier,

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:53.710
but I stopped somewhere on the way.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:57.460
<b>National
Admission Ticket

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:57.070
Movie tickets?

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:01.200
I thought we could go see it 
instead of that other movie.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:04.000
It might not be your favorite 
kind of movie, but...

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.990
You don't have to say yes!

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:07.470
If you say no, I'll see it on my own.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:10.510
I'm going! I'm definitely going!

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:11.800
I s-see...

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:18.800
B-But what's gotten into you?

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:21.520
You were mad this morning.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:27.430
Well, I didn't realize how
 my words affected you.

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.330
I realized I'd done something bad.

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.380
I'm really sorry.

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:33.630
I went too far, too.

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:36.740
I'm sorry. I should've calmed 
down instead of yelling.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:39.990
And I shouldn't say, "Die," 
even if I'm joking.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:42.110
Yeah, so...

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:43.960
Let's just both admit we were wrong.

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.520
Yeah.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:50.100
Um...

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.470
The miso soup!

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:55.640
Hey, are you okay?

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:58.340
It wouldn't suit you at all.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.850
Huh? What?

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:04.860
I was just thinking how weird 
you'd look in a frilly skirt.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.150
You're not really the feminine type.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.810
You're better off in shorts.

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:13.280
A blouse with a ribbon on it, or a dress, 
none of that stuff is good for you.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:17.080
Honestly, even seeing you in a 
school sailor uniform is weird.

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:20.550
You might look better wearing my uniform.

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:25.200
What are you even talking about?

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:26.690
Are you picking a fight with me?

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:27.960
You suck!

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:31.010
I was an idiot to expect 
any kind of tact from you!

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:32.760
Stupid Kei! Die!

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:35.250
You just told me to die again!

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:35.930
Shut up!

00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:38.130
I hate you! Don't even talk to me.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:40.260
Go to work or wherever!

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:30.340
Next time on <i>Girly Air Force</i>...

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:33.970
ALT 09: "Unphysical Layer."

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>Unphysical Layer</i>

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:37.600
Barbie 01, cleared for take off!
